  - learning-loop
  - observability
body: '## Cross-Study Sources\n\n- **OpenSpace** (HKUDS) — Self-evolving skill engine. 2k stars. Persistent, versionable, shareable skills with DAG lineage. 46% token reduction, 4.2x income on GDPVal benchmark.\n- **AnyTool** (HKUDS) — Universal tool-use layer. Progressive filtering pipeline (BM25 → semantic → LLM → quality penalty). Solves context pollution at 10,000+ tools.\n- **ClawWork** (HKUDS) — Economic survival benchmark. Agents start with $10, must earn through quality work. Quality gate at 0.6, BLS wage grounding, work/learn tradeoff.\n- **World Monitor** (koala73) — Real-time global intelligence. 45k stars. 30+ source correlation, per-source staleness, intelligence gap narration, convergence-over-volume scoring.\n\n## Top-Tier Takeaways\n\n1. Outcome-based learning metrics (OpenSpace + ClawWork)\n2. Token cost tracking per orchestration unit (ClawWork)\n3. Semantic tool retrieval pipeline (AnyTool)\n4. Intelligence gap narration (World Monitor)\n5. Skill lineage DAG — FIX/DERIVE/CAPTURE (OpenSpace)\n6. Per-subsystem staleness thresholds (World Monitor)\n\n## Second-Tier Takeaways\n\n7. Quality-gated workflow progression (ClawWork)\n8. Convergence scoring in ripple analysis (World Monitor)\n9. Pure-functional analysis core (World Monitor)\n10. Fuzzy symbol ID correction (OpenSpace)\n11. Staleness metadata in MCP responses (World Monitor)\n12. Adaptive agent behavior based on session health (ClawWork)\n13. Meta-tools for tool introspection (AnyTool)\n14. Two-phase execution with clean reset (OpenSpace)\n15. Negative-caching sentinel values (World Monitor)\n\n## Competitive Position\n\nParadigm''s moat: structured codebase context (symbols, purpose, portal) + multi-agent orchestration. No other system combines both.\nParadigm''s gaps: outcome-based learning, token cost tracking, semantic tool retrieval. All addressable.'
